  "node_id": "prop_13",
  "edition": "Newton, Principia, Andrew Motte trans., 1729 (Wikisource); Book I, Section III, Proposition XIII; Plate 5, Figure 3.",
  "caption": "If a body moves in the perimeter of a parabola, find the law of the centripetal force tending to the focus.",
  "n_steps": 4,
  "steps": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "gloss": "A body moves on a parabola with force directed to the focus S."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "gloss": "From the next place Q draw QR parallel to SP, QT perpendicular, and Qv parallel to the tangent."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "gloss": "Similar triangles give QR = Pv, and the conic property gives Qv squared = 4PS times QR."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "gloss": "As Q meets P the ratio Qv to Qx tends to unity, yielding force reciprocal to SP squared."
    }
  ],
